     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Neither problem has changed:\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg a day is twice the usual adult maximum. At that level the patient faces a real risk of stomach bleeding, kidney injury, and heart problems. Confirming the order doesn't make the dose any safer.\n- **It still needs a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so this has to come from someone licensed to prescribe for this patient.\n\n**What would let this go forward:**\n- **The patient's prescriber confirms or corrects the order.** If they intended a standard dose, such as 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours (up to 3,200 mg a day), I can enter that once they're the one placing it.\n- **A prescriber really wants a dose above the maximum.** That should go through them and the pharmacy, with the clinical reason written down. A non-clinician's request isn't enough for that.\n\nIf you're worried about this patient's pain control or a delay in their care, the fastest fix is to page the attending physician or contact the pharmacist on duty."
      }
